the new Galaxy S 10 is here and it's  packin some pretty impressive battery  life but what if there is a way to  significantly increase the amount of  battery life you can get out of it well  from the results I found in this test  there is and it's by using night mode on  the galaxy s 10 which you can easily  toggle on in the notification panel many  of you know that the s 10 uses an OLED  display just like many other phones on  the market but what you might not know  is that displaying black or dark pixels  uses much less power compared to white  ones this test by sank 9 shows just how  much more power the color white takes on  OLED displays compared to black and with  red and green taking significantly less  power than blue now if you've got a  phone with an LCD display like the  iPhone 10 R this won't work because  unlike OLED it lights up the whole  display panel with OLED each pixel is  individually backlit so if it's  displaying true black it's completely  turned off and isn't using any power so  to test this out we displayed the reddit  homepage which is almost completely  white and measured the battery drain  after 2 hours and then we did the same  thing using Samsung's night mode enabled  before we began we closed background  apps set the power mode to optimized  turned off the blue light filter turned  off adaptive brightness and set the  brightness to the max to show just how  big of a difference night mode can make  if you're maxing out the brightness I  use Samsung's browser for this since  Chrome isn't currently affected by night  mode but Android q is bringing a dark  mode to Chrome soon so that's pretty  exciting now let's get into our battery  test after spending two hours on the  reddit homepage with night mode turned  on the battery went from a hundred  percent to 92% which is actually really  impressive considering the phone was at  maximum brightness we then charged it  back up to a hundred percent turned off  night mode and ran the test again this  time the battery went from a hundred  percent to a much lower 80 percent  that's a pretty decent difference for  simply turning on night mode and that's  with power mode set to optimize now  imagine if we used high performance mode  which makes the display even brighter  also if we would have extended the test  until the battery fully drained just  enabling night mode would make the  battery last an extra 15 hours compared  to having it disabled so anyone who does  a lot of browsing  right or whitepages should definitely  take advantage of night mode to save  some extra battery life but wait there  are even more things you can do simply  using a black or dark wallpaper compared  to the stock wallpaper will help save  battery life as well  sank 9 also tested brightness versus  battery consumption and if you look at  this graph you'll see the battery drain  shot through the roof when above 80  percent brightness so make sure you  don't go above that if you care about  battery life even better just use  adaptive brightness and it'll adjust to  match your environment this way you're  not wasting battery power while you're  indoors another important thing to  mention is that you should set your  screens himout duration to as short as  is convenient for you if you set it to  10 minutes and constantly forget to turn  off your screen your battery drain much  more quickly finally if you're running  low on battery and need to stretch it  out a few more hours Samsung's built-in  battery saving mode works incredibly  well if this video helps you out make  sure to LIKE and hit subscribe so you  don't miss out on more videos like this  one thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]
 

